# Network git and CI

| Ref | Means |
|-----|-------|
| `main` | Prod config SoT (`sync-prod.yml` commits here) |
| `dev` | Twin captured state — force-pushed by `sync-dev.yml` / `reconcile-dev.yml` |
| review branch | Proposed change after twin validation |

Never develop on `dev`. Tags on `main` read as SoT events. `inventory/runtime/`
is ephemeral.

Judge Actions from the **job-log report marker prefix**, not the green check.

| Workflow | Writes | Marker prefix |
|----------|--------|----------------|
| `test.yml` | nothing | `# Network test report` |
| `sync-prod.yml` | `main` | `# Config collect report` |
| `sync-dev.yml` | force-push `dev` | `# Sync Dev report` |
| `deploy-twin.yml` | new CML lab | `# Deploy twin report` |
| `reconcile-dev.yml` | existing Dev + `dev` | `# Reconcile Dev report` |
| `detect-drift.yml` | nothing | `# Config drift report` |

`sync-dev.yml` has no `devices` input. `deploy-twin.yml` defaults
`tags=tag:simulate`. Twin owns those two topology workflows as intents; Sync
triggers them when named. Selectors: `tag:sync` (config), `tag:simulate`
(topology), `tag:patch` (design proposal). Always include `tag:`.
